    {
      "question": "e-7024",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/problem",
      "old_sha256": "e1cb3386f5af3f204f662a58b6f4c7ca21defa4578fdf353e7e3169d13efacc4",
      "new_sha256": "48d57db3f896e5f1cb762c5734281947d006272323b5b14316c1c57d596bbf77",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-7024",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $x=0,$ $y=0,$ and the curve $y=\\sqrt{4 - x^2}.$ What is $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_D (x+y)\\,\\mathrm{d}A$ expressed as a repeated integral?",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/example-7024.json",
          "file_sha256": "66b7ac248f2e9830fea14b624cbc421a8d3b9577f0d902b983511424ba68e320"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 1803,
      "reason": "Observed MA content supersedes the stored value",
      "action": "replace",
      "transaction_receipt": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/edb-import/commit.edn",
      "basis_after": 1804
    },
    {
      "question": "e-7024",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "ce2f87e81b51961cbd33213b3d3ed2df38c93aee974280f194e66c2014c99658",
      "new_sha256": "a901c1ac9359ab4e022c4a36daeb39230c3ac842ef49d4c0b0331e1cba081681",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-7024",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/3d67d73d3ede011d6c2fe4bc9e160aa3c2af522bff6cddfcc7c351c97418e764.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x  \\leq 2, \\quad 0 \\leq y \\leq \\sqrt{4-x^2} \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}(x+y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/example-7024.json",
          "file_sha256": "66b7ac248f2e9830fea14b624cbc421a8d3b9577f0d902b983511424ba68e320"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 1803,
      "reason": "Observed MA content supersedes the stored value",
      "action": "replace",
      "transaction_receipt": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/edb-import/commit.edn",
      "basis_after": 1804
