    {
      "question": "e-7026",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "e2a9eb819f577769344e5e737600e69a7ed099f638731f740c3a74b6b938e340",
      "new_sha256": "d1f620bb795df7078532d6b955fd4092a938d136530bec6afedc198fed4db772",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-7026",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}y\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{4}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{4}\\,dx & =\\frac{1}{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{5}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/example-7026.json",
          "file_sha256": "cdb24f986ffde3311e352c2c28daf4342ab576b8b25e0f2547bc6cd3a811633b"
        }
